Stop declaring DATABASE_URL in the Blueprint so it can be set in the dashboard

The value never reached the app: the boot log kept saying
"Database : sqlite:////opt/render/project/src/api/data/library.db" and the
service's Environment page showed the key missing, even though the same edit
happily deleted DATA_DIR.

Cause: a key declared in render.yaml is *managed by the Blueprint*, and Render
discards values typed into the dashboard for managed keys. `sync: false` only
prompts during the initial Blueprint creation, so there is no way to supply it
afterwards — the key was unusable.

DATABASE_URL is now absent from render.yaml, with a comment explaining why and
what to set in Dashboard -> service -> Environment. DEPLOY.md step 5.3 documents
the corrected procedure.

Verified end to end against a real Supabase Postgres beforehand: seeded the
catalogue, uploaded a track with cover art, streamed a byte range, then deleted
the whole local data/ directory and restarted — the track still listed, streamed
(206, 0-4095/1523659) and served its artwork.
